                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Pocatello ID",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 17 at 11:32AM MDT until September 17 at 1:00PM MDT by NWS Pocatello ID",
                "description": "At 1132 AM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nmoderate to heavy rain over the Big Rock Burn Scar have subsided at\nthe moment. However, there can be a delay between rainfall ending and\nany ongoing or potential flooding subsiding.  Other showers and\nthunderstorms with rainfall rates exceeding 0.25 inches may impact\nthe burn scar in the next 60 to 90 minutes.  Flash flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly. This will result in debris\nflows consisting of rock, mud, vegetation and other loose materials.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding in and around the Big Rock Burn Scar.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nBig Rock Burn Scar.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nHeise.",
                "instruction": "This is a life threatening situation. Heavy rainfall will cause\nextensive and severe flash flooding of creeks...streams...and ditches\nin the Big Rock Burn Scar. Severe debris flows can also be\nanticipated across roads. Roads and driveways may be washed away in\nplaces. If you encounter flood waters...climb to safety.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
