                "senderName": "NWS Northern Indiana",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 17 at 12:21PM EDT until September 17 at 2:15PM EDT by NWS Northern Indiana",
                "description": "At 1221 PM EDT, Doppler radar estimates between 2 and 5 inches of\nrain have fallen. Rain rates of one tenth to oen quarter of an inch\nper hour will be possible through 130 PM EDT. Additional rainfall\namounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are possible in the warned area. Flash\nflooding is already occurring. There have been several reports from\nearlier this morning of flooded roadways and stranded cards due to\nflood waters.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Trained spotters reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams, urban\nareas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nHuntington, Bluffton, Decatur, Berne, Ossian, Geneva, Andrews,\nMarkle, Monroe, Lancaster, Preble, Nottingham, Zanesville,\nWillshire, Uniondale, Wren, Poneto, Vera Cruz, Murray and North\nOaks.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.",
                "response": "Avoid",
